WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:14.806
No one, not even Jo herself, could deny that she had a short temper.

2
00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:22.406
That however, normally meant that whatever angered her was quickly forgotten, and the good-natured Jo prevailed once again.

3
00:00:22.407 --> 00:00:25.178
But this time was a different matter.

4
00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:34.421
Nothing anyone said, not even Mother's tender comforting words, could soothe the burning pain in Jo's heart.

5
00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:39.229
"I will never forgive her," Jo sobbed into Mother's arms.

6
00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:46.887
"I know you are very angry at this moment," Mother sympathized, "but don't utter words you may regret later."

7
00:00:46.888 --> 00:00:50.690
Inside, Mother's heart wept with her second child.

8
00:00:50.691 --> 00:00:57.275
Jo's beauty and charm, unlike Meg's or Amy's, was not immediately obvious to others.

9
00:00:57.276 --> 00:01:02.792
Her strength came from deep inside her creative soul and shone in her writing.

10
00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:09.511
This particular story was even more important to Jo because it was dedicated to her father.

11
00:01:09.512 --> 00:01:18.550
To Jo, taking and destroying her story was the same as cold-heartedly stabbing her in the back then cruelly laughing at her.

12
00:01:18.551 --> 00:01:25.494
"Even if I forgive Amy," Jo sniffed, "I don't think I will ever forget what she did."

13
00:01:25.495 --> 00:01:33.416
Mother held Jo close and silently prayed that this matter would not ruin the relationship between her two daughters forever.

14
00:01:33.417 --> 00:01:38.048
For the next couple of days Jo avoided Amy altogether.

15
00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:47.492
When they happened to come across each other, perhaps at mealtimes, Jo stared at her coldly and moved away as if Amy had some contagious disease.

16
00:01:47.493 --> 00:01:52.847
Amy found this chilly treatment far more painful than being slapped or pinched by her sister.

17
00:01:52.848 --> 00:02:00.712
On several occasions Amy tried to catch Jo off guard when she happened to be in a somewhat good mood or at least smiling.

18
00:02:00.713 --> 00:02:08.943
Each time, however, she was unsuccessful because Jo immediately stiffened and cooled when she saw Amy anywhere near her.

19
00:02:08.944 --> 00:02:13.543
One afternoon, Laurie came over to cheer up his downhearted buddy.

20
00:02:13.544 --> 00:02:22.855
At first Jo refused to accept what Laurie called his "special remedy" for the troubled heart─a good cry, a good laugh, and a good friend.

21
00:02:22.856 --> 00:02:27.714
But later she changed her mind when she realized that Laurie did make her happier.

22
00:02:27.715 --> 00:02:32.522
"See? It's not too difficult to smile, is it?" Laurie teased.

23
00:02:32.523 --> 00:02:38.026
"I'm not smiling; I'm frowning because you're making my head ache," Jo muttered,

24
00:02:38.027 --> 00:02:41.812
turning her head away to hide the corners of her mouth turning upward.

25
00:02:41.813 --> 00:02:48.433
"I have just the thing for headaches!" Laurie shot his finger up as if he had just thought of a brilliant idea.

26
00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:56.426
"Oh no," moaned Jo. "With all your remedies, you should be a doctor; not an artist, when you grow up, dear boy."

27
00:02:56.427 --> 00:03:02.138
Flapping his hand to silence her, Laurie simply said, "Fresh air."

28
00:03:02.139 --> 00:03:05.524
"I beg your pardon?" Jo laughed.

29
00:03:05.525 --> 00:03:08.764
"You need fresh air to get rid of that headache!

30
00:03:08.765 --> 00:03:13.130
And I know the best place for it," Laurie nodded knowingly.

31
00:03:13.131 --> 00:03:17.819
"Whatever you say, Dr. Laurie," replied the obedient patient.

32
00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:23.575
"Get your skates and meet me at my house," said Laurie, as he reached for the door handle.

33
00:03:23.576 --> 00:03:29.097
"Oh, skating! Why didn't I think of that! I'll be over in two seconds!"

34
00:03:29.098 --> 00:03:33.261
Jo clapped her hands excitedly and ran out of the room.

35
00:03:33.262 --> 00:03:40.792
If Jo had turned around as she crossed the living room, she would have caught sight of Amy, pretending to be interested in a book,

36
00:03:40.793 --> 00:03:44.382
but secretly listening to their conversation.

37
00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:48.258
Jo, however, was too excited to notice anything.

38
00:03:48.259 --> 00:03:54.103
In the woods behind the March house and Laurence mansion was a pond that froze over every winter.

39
00:03:54.104 --> 00:03:57.639
Some years it was even safe to skate on.

40
00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:04.847
"Brookes says the ice may not be thick enough in the middle but we should be able to skate along the edges," Laurie pointed out.

41
00:04:04.848 --> 00:04:08.144
"I'm not afraid. Are you?" Jo asked.

42
00:04:08.145 --> 00:04:16.705
"Of course not," Laurie replied hotly, "but we should be careful because the water will be freezing cold if you fall in."

43
00:04:16.706 --> 00:04:20.215
Jo tied the laces on her skates and stood up.

44
00:04:20.216 --> 00:04:24.659
"I'll race you around the pond. Loser has to carry the winner home!"

45
00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.327
With that Jo sped off, letting out a loud yell.

46
00:04:28.328 --> 00:04:31.771
Laurie hurriedly tied his laces and shot after her.

47
00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:40.129
Amy was relieved to see Jo behaving more like her usual self, though she still disapproved of her sister's tomboyish ways.

48
00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:45.729
Amy quickly put on her skates, determined to corner Jo while Laurie was around.

49
00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:51.876
She felt confident that this would be the day that Jo would forgive her so they could be at peace once again.

50
00:04:51.877 --> 00:04:56.887
"Jo!" she called out to the small figures on the opposite side of the pond.

51
00:04:56.888 --> 00:05:04.004
Hearing her name, Jo looked up but when she saw who was calling, her smile quickly turned into a scowl.

52
00:05:04.005 --> 00:05:08.025
She stopped abruptly, nearly causing Laurie to crash into her.

53
00:05:08.026 --> 00:05:12.355
"What's the matter?" Laurie cried breathlessly.

54
00:05:12.356 --> 00:05:19.299
"What is she doing here?" Jo pointed irritably to her sister who waved while trying to balance on her skates.

55
00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.753
Amy wobbled on her feet and carefully stepped onto the icy pond.

56
00:05:23.754 --> 00:05:29.270
Unfortunately for her, she hadn't heard Laurie's warnings about the middle of the pond.

57
00:05:29.271 --> 00:05:37.966
Wanting to reach Jo and Laurie as quickly as possible, Amy began to skate toward them, cutting across the center of the pond.

58
00:05:37.967 --> 00:05:42.337
"Oh no! Amy! Stop! Don't skate there!" Laurie shouted.

59
00:05:42.338 --> 00:05:45.715
Amy could not hear exactly what Laurie was shouting.

60
00:05:45.716 --> 00:05:49.004
Her only focus was on reaching Jo.

61
00:05:49.005 --> 00:05:56.005
"Amy! Stop! Go around the edge of the pond!" Jo cried, swinging her arms frantically.

62
00:05:56.006 --> 00:06:02.246
What happened next occurred in a flash, but to Jo everything seemed in slow motion.

63
00:06:02.247 --> 00:06:10.531
Amy tilted forward as if she had tripped over something, then she glanced down and immediately jerked her head up, searching for an escape.

64
00:06:10.532 --> 00:06:16.469
Jo heard a slight cracking noise like distant thunder, followed by a splash.

65
00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:23.744
"Amy!" Jo screamed as she saw her sister disappear rapidly beneath the icy waters.

66
00:06:23.745 --> 00:06:28.104
Everything that had happened between her and Amy vanished from Jo's thoughts

67
00:06:28.105 --> 00:06:33.569
as the only fear that gripped her now was that she might never see her little sister again.

68
00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:40.258
Jo started to skate toward the hole Amy had fallen into, but Laurie grabbed her before she could go any further.

69
00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:47.732
"It's too dangerous," he spun his head around and located a large fallen branch. "Help me with this!"

70
00:06:47.733 --> 00:06:53.942
Laurie and Jo got the branch and carefully skated closer to where Amy's head was bobbing in and out of the water.

71
00:06:53.953 --> 00:07:01.204
"Amy! Grab this! We'll pull you out!" Jo yelled as she and Laurie pushed the branch toward the hole.

72
00:07:01.205 --> 00:07:07.372
Somehow Amy heard her sister's instructions and grasped the branch with her cold, weak hands.

73
00:07:07.373 --> 00:07:13.706
"Hold tightly!" Laurie shouted, as he and Jo pulled Amy out of the freezing waters.

74
00:07:13.707 --> 00:07:20.662
When they had gotten Amy to safer ground, Jo threw her own coat over Amy's shivering little body.

75
00:07:20.663 --> 00:07:26.532
Laurie did the same, even taking off his wool sweater and covering Amy's head with it.

76
00:07:26.533 --> 00:07:31.809
"We have to get her home, now!" Laurie said in an unusually authoritative voice.

77
00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:34.440
Jo was not about to argue with her friend.

78
00:07:34.441 --> 00:07:43.302
She was glad that someone was taking charge of the situation, because she had never felt so helpless in all her life.
